  "name": "Cryo Refraction",
  "type": "spell",
  "effects": [],
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\">You summon a magical crystal that resonates when it is struck. You choose the elemental nature of this crystal when you summon it in the target area, whether it is made of Cold, Force, Air or Earth energy. The crystal covers approximately the size of a large creature, and provides lesser cover, has an AC of 10, 60 hit points, and a hardness of 10. It possesses object immunities, and resistance 10 to Cold, Force, Air and Earth.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Each time you Sustain this spell or a creature damages the crystal, it loses at least 20 hit points, even if it would take less damage. When it takes damage, it unleashes a 15-foot cone of energy of its type from a corner, dealing 4d6 damage against a basic Reflex save to creatures in the cone. If an ally damages the crystal, they decide the corner and direction of the cone. If you Sustain, or either you or an enemy damages the crystal, you decide.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">When the crystal reaches 0 hit points or the duration of the spell elapses, it falls apart harmlessly as the spell ends. You can Dismiss this spell.</p><hr><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The hit points of the crystal increases by 10 and its hardness and resistances increases by 2. The damage of the cone blasts increases by 1d6.</p>"
    },
